From 22ed04085ea0d7590415be7121f9e8fb5e7358df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 04:49:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 102/112] Output limiter (Community features, off by default):
 a look-ahead peak limiter with a soft knee before the output clips

Switched on (Community features > Output limiter, 7-segment LIMT, saved in CommunityFeatures.XML as outputLimiter),
the render buffer passes a look-ahead peak limiter (dsp/output_limiter.h) as its last stage before the output's
hard clip: the knee starts 1 dB below full scale and flattens out just under it (f(p) = T + (C-T) v/sqrt(1+v^2)),
the gain is the lowest asked for over the next 33 samples, held 15 ms, released over 60 ms, averaged over 32
samples (the attack), stereo-linked, on the input delayed by 32 samples (0.73 ms latency while on). No sample
reaches full scale; the gain moves smoothly, so no harmonics to alias (a 2x oversampled soft clipper only took a
hard clip's aliasing down by 7-10 dB at 5-11 kHz). Below the knee the output is the input bit for bit (delayed).
Off, it doesn't run: the output is exactly as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eb214cM1zi1k5Gpcn9RLKh
